   796	\subsection{\TDDED}
   797	\label{sec:tdiamond}
   798	
   799	We recall that $t$-diamond is the graph $K_2+tK_1$ and that 
   800	2-diamond is the diamond graph. Clearly, $t$-diamond is a sparse $(\ell, h)$-degree graph.
   801	In this subsection, we prove that \TDDED\ is \NPC. Further, we 
   802	prove that the problem cannot be solved in parameterized subexponential time,
   803	unless ETH fails. We use an inductive proof where the base case is \DED.
   804	For the proof, we introduce a simple construction, which is 
   805	given below.
   806	
   807	
   808	\begin{figure}[h]
   809	  \centering
   810	  \includegraphics[width=1.0in]{diamond.pdf}
   811	  \caption{A 2-diamond is isomorphic to a diamond graph.}
   812	  \label{fig:diamond}
   813	\end{figure}
